window.products.push({"id":581671,"name":"HAPI design Turtle Foldable Storage Box with Side Handlers","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/81JdIRwob+L._SL1500_.jpg","description":"Keep your children’s room organized with foldable storage box Bringing up a baby is a herculean task. However, more difficult is keeping the kid’s room organized. From clothes to diapers, from rattles to balls and cars, you would be surprised by the amount of things your baby needs. The problem arises when you cannot find the right thing at the right moment. Getting organized with a baby’s stuff would make your life a lot easier and stress-free. We present foldable storage boxes that are convenient, beautiful and can help you to keep your children’s room perfectly organized. Foldable storage box – the perfect solution to your organizing issues Our foldable storage boxes with side handlers are absolute must if you have kids at home. You can store all their belongings in these boxes. They are ideal to stock clothes and toys. Put all the little things in it and keep the room well organized.  With cute and delightful images of turtle and zebra, these boxes are ideal for a kid’s room. They add color to the décor and even the kids would love to look at them.  The side handlers make it easy for you to shift the boxes. Simply fold the box and keep it away when you want more space in the room. Otherwise use the box to throw in the things in it and keep the room clean. It would be easy for you to take out the clothes or toys when you need them.  The reinforced bottom makes the boxes sturdy enough to hold a lot of stuff. Made from good quality material, the foldable storage box makes a good gift item. Gift it to a would-be-mom on baby shower to store all the gifts she would be receiving.  The white colored boxes with cutesy pictures would complement any home décor. They are functional, convenient and give every home a colorful touch. Make your children’s room come alive with our foldable storage box.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/81JdIRwob+L._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Amazon marketplace","source_asin":"B01CSAXFUG","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-581671","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B01CSAXFUG","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B01CSAXFUG","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
window.products.push({"id":581672,"name":"Manual Woodworkers & Weavers Table Runner, Coastal Jewels","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41Vc+MQY-0L._AC_SL1020_.jpg","description":"A refreshing mix of sea shells adorn this design by Lisa Audit. Made in the USA. Look for Manual's extensive line of home decor, tapestries, wall hangings, women's fashion accessories and more. Although Thomas Lemuel Oates started Manual Woodworkers & Weavers in 1932, the story goes back further. The roots of the company can be found in Oates' entrepreneurial spirit. He and his brother used to farm the mountain areas of Bat Cave in western North Carolina. They would also help their mother find materials for her crafts. The sons began to make wooden whistles, buckets and bird-houses. They would sell their wares along with her crafts to the people from Charlotte that came through in their horse-drawn buggies on the way to the mountains. Later, Thomas worked at the Ashville Postcard Company. When the Depression hit, he lost his job, but it inspired him to go into business and sell crafts, like cornhusk dolls and woven pieces, that were produced by the local women. He had learned about the wholesale business while working at Ashville. He built a waterwheel to generate electricity at a mill, began making product and opened shop. Over the years, he expanded the company. His son, Lemuel Oates, who would next manage the company, says he worked in the business from a young age. He explains the products were made from cotton scraps left over from making socks. Half-inch circles would be looped together to form a variety of products. Lemuel Oates went to college and then settled in Richmond. In December 1973, he returned to Bat Cave and took over the company. In 2007 his son Travis and his daughter, Molly Oates Sherrill, took over the business.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41Vc+MQY-0L._AC_SL1020_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Manual","source_asin":"B00J1RBO2G","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-581672","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B00J1RBO2G","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B00J1RBO2G","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
